{
  "info": {
    "name": "Folderly API (Auth + Users + S3 Uploads + Reports)",
    "description": "Postman collection for the secure Node.js/Express/MongoDB API.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Import this collection.\n2. Edit *collection variables*: `baseUrl`, `adminIdentifier`, `adminPassword` (the values from `npm run seed:admin`).\n3. Run **1. Auth -> Login - Admin** (token auto-saved).\n4. Run **2. Users -> Create user** (saves `userId`).\n5. Run **1. Auth -> Login - User** to test as the normal user, then **3. Uploads** and **4. Reports**.\n6. Run **5. RBAC & security checks** as the normal user to verify protections.\n\nAll authenticated requests use the collection-level Bearer token `{{accessToken}}`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000",
      "description": "API origin (no trailing slash)"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminIdentifier",
      "value": "admin",
      "description": "Admin username or email"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "ChangeMe#12345",
      "description": "Admin password"
    },
    {
      "key": "userIdentifier",
      "value": "riya",
      "description": "Normal user's username/email"
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "Str0ng#Passw0rd!",
      "description": "Normal user's password"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-set by login requests"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-set by Create user"
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-set by Upload files"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "description": "Liveness probe. No authentication.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns `{status:'ok'}`. Use for load-balancer / uptime checks. **Note:** this is outside `/api/v1`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Authentication endpoints.\n\n**How tokens work**\n- `accessToken` (JWT, 15 min) is returned in the JSON body and sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. The collection saves it automatically into `{{accessToken}}`.\n- The refresh token is an **httpOnly cookie** (`refresh_token`, path `/api/v1/auth`). Postman's cookie jar stores and sends it automatically - you never handle it manually.\n- There is **no public signup**. Only an admin can create users.\n\n**Switching identity:** run *Login - Admin* or *Login - User*; whichever you ran last sets `{{accessToken}}` used by every other request.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login - Admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in using username **or** email in `identifier`.\n\n- Success: `200` with `user`, `accessToken`, `expiresIn`; sets refresh cookie.\n- Wrong credentials: `401 Invalid credentials` (same message for unknown user / wrong password).\n- 5 failed attempts: account locked for 15 min -> `423`.\n- Rate limited to 10 requests / 15 min / IP -> `429`.\n\nSet `adminIdentifier` / `adminPassword` collection variables first (the values you used in `npm run seed:admin`).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{adminIdentifier}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "pm.test('Role is admin', () => pm.expect(d.user.role).to.eql('admin'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same as above but for the normal user you created in *Users -> Create user*. Uses `userIdentifier` / `userPassword` variables.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{userIdentifier}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', d.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh access token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uses the **refresh_token cookie** (sent automatically) to issue a new access token and **rotate** the refresh cookie.\n\n- Reusing an old (already rotated) refresh token is treated as theft: the whole session family is revoked -> `401`.\n- No body needed.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', pm.response.json().data.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user (me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the authenticated user's profile (never includes password hash)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Change my password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "change-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Changes the logged-in user's own password. **All sessions are revoked** - you must login again.\n\nPassword policy: 12-72 chars, upper + lower + number + special, must differ from the current one.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"OldPassw0rd!234\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewStr0ng#Passw0rd\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout (this device)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Ends the current session: revokes the refresh-token family (cookie) **and** the session behind the Bearer access token, so the access token stops working immediately (`/auth/me` -> 401). Clears the cookie."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout all devices",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout-all",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "logout-all"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Revokes **every** session of the current user. All their access tokens stop working immediately."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Users (Admin only)",
      "description": "User management. Every request here requires an **admin** access token (run *Login - Admin* first). Non-admins get `403`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Admin creates a user.\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|---|---|\n| name | 2-100 chars |\n| username | 3-30 chars, `a-z 0-9 _ -` (used in the S3 folder path) |\n| email | valid email |\n| password | 12-72 chars, upper+lower+number+special |\n| role | `admin`, `marketing`, `sales`, `hr`, `finance`, `support` |\n\nUnknown fields are rejected (`400`). Duplicate username/email -> `409`. The new user's id is saved to `{{userId}}`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Riya Sharma\",\n  \"username\": \"riya\",\n  \"email\": \"riya@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng#Passw0rd!\",\n  \"role\": \"marketing\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', pm.response.json().data.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "marketing",
                  "description": "Filter by role",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "isActive",
                  "value": "true",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "riya",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paginated list. Optional filters: `role`, `isActive` (true/false), `search` (matches name/username/email), `page`, `limit` (max 100)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{userId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fetch one user by Mongo id."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update user",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{userId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Update `name`, `role` and/or `isActive` (at least one). Changing role or deactivating **revokes the user's sessions**. An admin cannot change their own role or deactivate themselves (`400`).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Riya S.\",\n  \"role\": \"sales\",\n  \"isActive\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset user password (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/reset-password",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{userId}}",
                "reset-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Admin sets a new password for a user, clears any lockout, and revokes all their sessions.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"newPassword\": \"Another#Str0ngPass1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Deactivate user",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{userId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Soft-delete: sets `isActive=false` and revokes sessions. The user's files and report history are kept."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Uploads (S3)",
      "description": "File uploads to S3. Any authenticated role can upload. Files are stored at **`ROLE/USERNAME/YYYY-MM-DD/<uuid>-<filename>`** inside the configured bucket.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Upload files",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`multipart/form-data`, field name must be **`files`** (up to 5 per request, 10 MB each by default).\n\nAllowed: pdf, png, jpg/jpeg, csv, txt, docx, xlsx. File **content** is verified (magic bytes), not just the extension.\n\nIn Postman: Body -> form-data -> `files` -> change type to **File** and choose file(s). Do **not** set Content-Type manually.\n\nErrors: `415` bad type/content, `413` too large, `400` no files. If any file fails, none are kept.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "files",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select one or more files"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "if (d.length) pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadId', d[0].id);",
                  "pm.test('Key follows ROLE/USERNAME/DATE', () => pm.expect(d[0].key).to.match(/^[a-z0-9_-]+\\/[a-z0-9_-]+\\/\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\//));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List my uploads",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/me?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads",
                "me"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-11-01",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-11-30",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns **only the logged-in user's** files. Filter by date range `from`/`to` (`YYYY-MM-DD`, based on the upload folder date)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List all uploads (Admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "userId",
                  "value": "{{userId}}",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "marketing",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-11-01",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-11-30",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Admin only. Filter by `userId`, `role`, `from`, `to`. Response includes `username` and `role` of each file."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get download link",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/{{uploadId}}/download",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads",
                "{{uploadId}}",
                "download"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a **presigned S3 URL** valid for 5 minutes (`SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS`). The bucket is private. Allowed for the file owner or an admin; anyone else gets `404` (not `403`) so ids can't be probed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Reports / Dashboard",
      "description": "All report endpoints accept optional `from` / `to` (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Default range is the **last 30 days**; max range is 366 days. Sizes (`bytes`) are in bytes.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "My report (any role)",
